{"name":"Adaptive Shade","hex":"#867e70","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adaptive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, characterized by or showing adaptation; making or made fit or suitable.","Capable of being adapted or of adapting; susceptible of or undergoing accordant change."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adaptive"},{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"adaptive":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-adaptive.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/76/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-adaptive.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-adaptive.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/76/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-adaptive.wav